#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0165 expect=violation domain=ADLB
#note "W5 (PLAN-grouped-aggregate-functions §2.4) — the CHAR-ranks-as-TEXT drift guard (D-W1-2a, D-W3-5). Subject 101/ALT carries TWO baseline-flagged rows (a duplicated ABLFL=Y, legal in data and the only way one group can hold two candidates) graded '9' and '10': as text '9' > '10', so $baseline_atoxgr = '9'; BTOXGR is '10' on every row, so all three populated rows fire ('10' != '9'). MEASURED 2026-09-29 on the pre-port engine (cumba-corej@8513690): GREEN — the retired evalMaxGrouped only took its numeric branch for cells whose getValueAsDouble() is finite, and DataValueString answers NaN for every real Char column, so text order was already the shipped answer and no verdict moves with the port (the ruling audit's premise that max parsed Char values numerically was measured false; only a computed STRING target, population 0, could reach that branch). Kept as the pin of the order the function must keep. A numeric order over a Char grade, where an authority means it, is the author's max(num(ATOXGR), …)."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 3
#expectViolationAt row=1 PARAMCD=ALT BASETYPE=LAST ATOXGR=9 BTOXGR=10 "$baseline_atoxgr"=9
#expectViolationAt row=2 PARAMCD=ALT BASETYPE=LAST ATOXGR=10 BTOXGR=10 "$baseline_atoxgr"=9
#expectViolationAt row=3 PARAMCD=ALT BASETYPE=LAST ATOXGR=2 BTOXGR=10 "$baseline_atoxgr"=9
dataset ADLB label="Analysis Dataset Lab"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD  type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col AVISITN  type=Num  label="Analysis Visit (N)"
col BASETYPE type=Char label="Baseline Type"
col ABLFL    type=Char label="Baseline Record Flag"
col ATOXGR   type=Char label="Analysis Toxicity Grade"
col BTOXGR   type=Char label="Baseline Toxicity Grade"
---
S1 | 101 | ALT | 0 | LAST | Y | 9  | 10
S1 | 101 | ALT | 0 | LAST | Y | 10 | 10
S1 | 101 | ALT | 1 | LAST |   | 2  | 10
